@startuml transaction-status
' transactionStatus for a single SEPA credit transfer — CTX-PAYMENT-INITIATION, INV-PAY-02/03.
' PROPOSAL, AI, 2026-09-19. Source: SRC-IG §4.14.1, §5.4, §14.13. Which path the bank reports
' after ACTC depends on its booking type (Q-28); both candidate paths are drawn.
title transactionStatus (single payment, proposal)

[*] --> RCVD : POST /v1/payments/sepa-credit-transfers
RCVD --> PDNG : optional (§4.14.1)
RCVD --> ACTC : authorisation finalised,\ntechnical checks passed
PDNG --> ACTC
RCVD --> RJCT : SCA not completed in time\nor authorisation failed
ACTC --> ACCP : customer profile checked\n(batch booking, type B)
ACTC --> ACSP : settlement started\n(real-time booking)
ACCP --> ACSC
ACSP --> ACSC : booked on debtor account
ACTC --> RJCT : e.g. FUNDS_NOT_AVAILABLE
ACTC --> CANC : cancelled (cancellation\nnot in MVP, Q-15)
RJCT --> [*]
ACSC --> [*]
CANC --> [*]

note as N1
  The XS2A interface need not report statuses reached after the initiation process (§4.14.1).
  VoP statuses RVCM / RVNC / RCVC (§14.13) are omitted until Q-16 is answered.
end note
@enduml
